issue_context.body:
**Describe the bug**

The response to a USB GET_INTERFACE is always 0, see the following excerpt from subsys/usb/usb_device.c. 

```
	case REQ_GET_INTERFACE:
		/* there is only one interface, return n-1 (= 0) */
		data[0] = 0U;
		*len = 1;
		break;
```
But according to USB Specification Revision 2.0 (usb_20.pdf from usb.org) section 9.4.4 GET_INTERFACE should return "selected alternate setting for the specified interface."

**To Reproduce**

There is no (or at least I can't find one that builds for my board) sample that has multiple USB alternate settings; but it is possible to reproduce using a patch to subsys/usb/class/loopback.c and samples/subsys/usb/testusb. 

1. Apply the following patch.

```
diff --git a/subsys/usb/class/loopback.c b/subsys/usb/class/loopback.c
index 754c2a4906..df35aee390 100644
--- a/subsys/usb/class/loopback.c
+++ b/subsys/usb/class/loopback.c
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ struct usb_loopback_config {
        struct usb_if_descriptor if0;
        struct usb_ep_descriptor if0_out_ep;
        struct usb_ep_descriptor if0_in_ep;
+       struct usb_if_descriptor if0_1;
 } __packed;

 USBD_CLASS_DESCR_DEFINE(primary, 0) struct usb_loopback_config loopback_cfg = {
@@ -65,6 +66,19 @@ USBD_CLASS_DESCR_DEFINE(primary, 0) struct usb_loopback_config loopback_cfg = {
                .wMaxPacketSize = sys_cpu_to_le16(CONFIG_LOOPBACK_BULK_EP_MPS),
                .bInterval = 0x00,
        },
+
+       .if0_1 = {
+               .bLength = sizeof(struct usb_if_descriptor),
+               .bDescriptorType = USB_INTERFACE_DESC,
+               .bInterfaceNumber = 0,
+               .bAlternateSetting = 1,
+               .bNumEndpoints = 0,
+               .bInterfaceClass = CUSTOM_CLASS,
+               .bInterfaceSubClass = 0,
+               .bInterfaceProtocol = 0,
+               .iInterface = 0,
+       },
+
 };
 /* usb.rst config structure end */
```
2. Build the testusb sample (my example below for the NXP RT1020 EVK). 

```
west build -p auto -b mimxrt1020_evk samples/subsys/usb/testusb
```
3. Flash.
4. Run USB Chapter 9 TEsts (USB 2 Devices) in the compliance tool from usb.org (USB 3 Gen X).

The test will fail in Configured State - TD 9.4 with an error message "A successful GetInterface request must return the alternate setting set by a prior call to SetInterface". 

**Expected behavior**

Compliance tests should pass.

**Environment (please complete the following information):**
 - OS: Ubuntu
 - Toolchain: Zephyr SDK 0.11.2
 - Zephyr master b74cad5a5d0f35905c4ab3d719bdc6b2794bc940.

