review_comments:
Tbh I am happy You mentioned that. I think I have an idea of how We can accomplish that.
Instead of `usb_cfg_data :: interfaces` with type of `const struct usb_if_descriptor *const *const` We can create a list of structs which not only points to interface but to alternate (if exists) as well + whatever we want to have there. Having that we will be able to "know" the configured function/class form core.

Simply speaking something like:
`usb_cfg_data :: const struct interface_container *const *const` 
Where `struct interface_container` is:
```
struct interface_container {
    struct usb_if_descriptor *iface;
    struct usb_if_descriptor *iface_alt;
    uint8_t curr_alt;
};
```
